<!--
Exemplar of the ROOT AGENTS.md of a generated project. Written in step 6 of SKILL.md with
{{projectName}} resolved and this comment dropped. A pointer, never an owner: every fact it
would carry already has one in the root CLAUDE.md or in a module AGENTS.md, and a second copy
here would drift (invariant 2 of Nerviz). Claude Code skips this file — the root has a
CLAUDE.md — so it is read only by the other agents: Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Jules, Aider,
and GitHub Copilot, which reads CLAUDE.md too. Design: decision 0139 of Nerviz.
-->

# {{projectName}} — instructions for coding agents

Read `CLAUDE.md`, at this root, before changing anything. It is written for every agent, not
only Claude Code: the stack, the build and test commands, the invariants, the module
structure, and its section "Under another agent", which says which of this project's checks
hold for you and which do not.

- **Norms** live in `.claude/rules/`, one topic per file; `.claude/rules/00-index.md` says
  which file covers what. Open the one your change touches.
{{#if moduleAgentFiles}}
- **Each module with import restrictions** has its own `AGENTS.md`, listing what that module
  may not import.
{{else}}
- **Import restrictions are per package**, not per module: `.claude/forbidden-imports.txt`
  lists each forbidden prefix with the package path it applies to.
{{/if}}
